# Memory Bank

This agent starts each session with no memory of prior chats. `memory-bank/` is the only durable project context. Read it before doing work. Keep it accurate.

## Naming

All Memory Bank files use **kebab-case** (`project-brief.md`, `active-context.md`, `specs/dev-plan.md`). Never create camelCase or undelimited names.

## Start of every task

Read all of these (extras required too):

- `memory-bank/project-brief.md`
- `memory-bank/product-context.md`
- `memory-bank/system-patterns.md`
- `memory-bank/tech-context.md`
- `memory-bank/github-pages.md`
- `memory-bank/multiplex.md`
- `memory-bank/active-context.md`
- `memory-bank/progress.md`
- `memory-bank/specs/dev-plan.md` (when implementing)

If a core file is missing, recreate it from the others and say so. Do not invent product scope that contradicts `project-brief.md`.

## Commands

- **initialize memory bank** — create or repair the files above from the repo + user intent.
- **update memory bank** — re-read every file, then update all that are stale. Always refresh `active-context.md` and `progress.md`.
- **follow your custom instructions** — read the bank and continue from `active-context.md` / `progress.md`.

## When to write the bank (without being asked)

Update after significant work: new patterns, architecture choices, scaffold/deploy milestones, or a change in next steps. Capture insights in the bank, not only in chat.

## File roles

| File | Role |
| --- | --- |
| `project-brief.md` | Scope source of truth |
| `product-context.md` | Why / who / UX |
| `system-patterns.md` | Architecture and component patterns |
| `tech-context.md` | Stack, tooling, constraints |
| `github-pages.md` | Static hosting and `base` path |
| `multiplex.md` | Live follow-along + Railway Socket.IO |
| `active-context.md` | Current focus (update most often) |
| `progress.md` | Done / todo / risks |
| `specs/` | Plans and acceptance criteria (`specs/dev-plan.md` = build order) |

Optional extra files under `memory-bank/` are allowed for features that do not fit the core set. New files must use kebab-case.

For the full initialize/update procedure, use the project skill `memory-bank`.
